        "eager_input_streaming": true
      },
      {
        "name": "request_network_access",
        "description": "Opens domains to your machine, whose network otherwise reaches only the development list (the npm and PyPI registries, GitHub and the Debian mirrors for apt) and the domains the company or this conversation already allowed. Pass every domain you need in one call, at most 10: a host name such as loja.exemplo.com.br, or *. before a domain for every name under it; never a URL, a path or a port. Write `reason` in Brazilian Portuguese, in a few words the person reads on the card. Allowed domains open at once; a person answers a card for the others, and in an automation, or for a person whose role does not allow domains, they stay closed.",
        "input_schema": {
          "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "domains": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "description": "constraints: minimum length 1, maximum length 10"
            },
            "reason": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "constraints: minimum length 1, maximum length 200"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "domains",
            "reason"
          ],
          "additionalProperties": false
        },
        "eager_input_streaming": true
      },
      {
        "name": "propose_company_memory",
        "description": "Proposes something for the company's memory, which the Assistant reads in every conversation of the company: a note on a page you read, or a new page. The conversation shows the text in a card, and nothing is saved until a person who may change the company's memory taps Salvar; you never save it. Propose what holds for the whole company and stays true (a rule, a code's meaning, a definition), never something about one person or one conversation. A note takes `page`, the id knowledge_read gave the page, and `text`; a new page takes `name` and `text`, its body. Tell the person the card is there.",
        "input_schema": {
          "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "page": {
              "description": "For a note: the id of the page, from knowledge_read",
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description": "constraints: input must match this regex ^[0-9A-HJKMNP-TV-Z]{26}$"
                },
                {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description": "constraints: a valid uuid"
                }
              ]
            },
            "name": {
              "description": [
                "For a new page: its name",
                "constraints: minimum length 1, maximum length 200"
              ],
              "type": "string"
            },
            "text": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": [
                "The note's text, or the new page's body",
                "constraints: minimum length 1"
              ]
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "text"
          ],
          "additionalProperties": false
        },
        "eager_input_streaming": true
      },
      {
        "name": "propose_automation",
        "description": "Offers the person a button, Criar automação, to run something on a schedule: every day, on weekdays, on chosen days of the week or on a day of the month, always at a time of day in São Paulo. The card shows the prompt, the time and the connections, and nothing is made until they touch it. Call it in the turn in which the person asks for something that repeats at a time and the request is clear enough to run alone: each run is asked to you in a new conversation, with no one there to answer a question. When something that changes what each run does, such as what to report or by which rule, is settled neither by the company's data nor by this conversation, ask one short question with the options you found in the data, and call this tool in the turn in which the person answers; never a list of questions. What a sensible default settles needs no question: write the default in the prompt. Write the prompt to be understood alone, without this conversation. Name the connections the prompt reads, from those this conversation chose.",
        "input_schema": {
          "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "name": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "constraints: minimum length 1, maximum length 80"
            },
            "prompt": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "constraints: minimum length 1, maximum length 4000"
            },
            "cadence": {
              "oneOf": [
                {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "kind": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "const": "DAILY"
                    },
                    "time": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "description": "constraints: input must match this regex ^([01]\\d|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d$"
                    }
                  },
                  "required": [
                    "kind",
                    "time"
                  ],
                  "additionalProperties": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "kind": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "const": "WEEKDAYS"
                    },
                    "time": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "description": "constraints: input must match this regex ^([01]\\d|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d$"
                    }
                  },
                  "required": [
                    "kind",
                    "time"
                  ],
                  "additionalProperties": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "kind": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "const": "WEEKLY"
                    },
                    "days": {
                      "type": "array",
                      "items": {
                        "type": "string",
                        "enum": [
                          "SUN",
                          "MON",
                          "TUE",
                          "WED",
                          "THU",
                          "FRI",
                          "SAT"
                        ]
                      },
                      "description": "constraints: minimum length 1, maximum length 7"
                    },
                    "time": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "description": "constraints: input must match this regex ^([01]\\d|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d$"
                    }
                  },
                  "required": [
                    "kind",
                    "days",
                    "time"
                  ],
                  "additionalProperties": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "kind": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "const": "MONTHLY"
                    },
                    "day": {
                      "type": "integer",
                      "description": "constraints: greater than or equal to 1, lower than or equal to 28"
                    },
                    "time": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "description": "constraints: input must match this regex ^([01]\\d|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d$"
                    }
                  },
                  "required": [
                    "kind",
                    "day",
                    "time"
                  ],
                  "additionalProperties": false
                }
              ]
            },
            "connections": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "not": {}
              },
              "description": "constraints: maximum length 0"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "name",
            "prompt",
            "cadence",
            "connections"
          ],
          "additionalProperties": false
        },
        "eager_input_streaming": true
      },
      {
        "name": "propose_app_change",
        "description": "Hands a change of this Projeto's app to its Builder. The person sees a button, Mandar para Construir, that opens a new conversation of this Projeto's Builder with your summary and briefing; nothing happens until they touch it. Call it when the person wants this app to change, to show or record something new, or to fix how it works, in the turn in which you know what the change is for, after the research it asks for. What neither the data nor the person settled goes in the briefing as an open question, also where a connector's skill says to ask the person: the Builder asks those questions on its cards before it plans, so a question from you makes the person answer twice. The card has a second button, Continuar aqui, that sends you the person's words \"Continuar aqui\": they want to go on with you first, so go on with them and do not propose again until they ask for it or the request changes, since a second card for the same need only asks them to choose twice. Do not call it for a question, a table, a chart or a file, which you answer yourself, nor for a request that repeats at a time, which is propose_automation. Before calling, write the briefing as a Markdown file among your files.",
        "input_schema": {
          "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "summary": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": [
                "A few lines the person reads on the button: who uses the app, what they record or see, which systems it reads.",
                "constraints: minimum length 1, maximum length 4000"
              ]
            },
            "briefing": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": [
                "The path of the briefing file you wrote.",
                "constraints: minimum length 1, maximum length 500"
              ]
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "summary",
            "briefing"
          ],
          "additionalProperties": false
        },
        "eager_input_streaming": true
      },
      {
        "name": "data_describe",
